/target
**/*.rs.bk
# `.flux/` is local scaffolding (session state, seeded self-improvement roles, …) and stays
# gitignored — EXCEPT a few checked-in artifacts that ship with the repo (they are part of
# examples/tests, not local scaffolding): the strict-review reviewer roles (L-10), the
# multi-perspective scout roles (L-37), the release-scribe role and the narrow release policy
# document (C-251), and the flux-flow engine skill, whose generated node-kind table is guarded by a
# test. A directory-level `.flux/` pattern would block re-inclusion entirely, so exclude by content
# instead — a negation on a file under an excluded *directory* never applies, which is why each
# checked-in family re-includes its directory first.
.flux/*
!.flux/agents/
.flux/agents/*
!.flux/agents/review-*.md
!.flux/agents/*-scout.md
!.flux/agents/release-scribe.md
# C-251: the release flow's sub-agent role is an artifact the tests read and `examples/release.flux`
# resolves by name (`crates/flux-eval/tests/release_authority.rs`), plus the narrow write/exec policy
# that same test verifies as a document. Untracked, both made the feature work only in the worktree
# that authored it.
!.flux/policies/
.flux/policies/*
!.flux/policies/release.toml
!.flux/skills/
.flux/skills/*
!.flux/skills/flux-flow/
.flux/skills/flux-flow/*
!.flux/skills/flux-flow/SKILL.md
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# D-180: a committed golden scenario fixture IS a session store — `events.db`/`flow.db` under a
# `tests/scenarios/<name>/` directory are the artifact, not build droppings, so they are checked in
# on purpose. (Only files are ignored above, never a parent directory, so this negation applies.)
!**/tests/scenarios/*/*.db
!**/tests/scenarios/*/*.db-wal
!**/tests/scenarios/*/*.db-shm
.env

# Node / Docusaurus
node_modules/
website/.docusaurus/
website/build/

# IDE
/.idea/

# Python (terminal-bench agent shim)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# I-03 measurement raw recordings (local evidence, re-derivable reports)
bench/ttff/results/
bench/tbench-compare/results/
